  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Data for Impact (D4I)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  USAID&apos;s Data for Impact (D4I) activity will provide technical support to local Bangladeshi public and non-governmental organizations to build their capacity to design and conduct rigorous program evaluations, specialized population-based surveys, data analysis, and implementation research using innovative and efficient approaches and tools. With FY 2023 funds, D4I will strengthen the use of data in decision-making at the Bangladesh Ministry of Health and Family Welfare (MOHFW) through the provision of a Technical Assistance Support Team to the Program Management and Monitoring Unit of the Planning Wing of MOHFW. Through D4I&apos;s technical advisors embedded in the MOHFW, D4I will facilitate the use of evidence to design Bangladesh&apos;s next five-year health sector program, expected to begin in 2024. D4I will partner with local organizations to assist with data analysis, research, and developing key policy documents to guide the MOHFW on evidence-based programming. D4I will continue to engage the media to raise awareness on priority health issues and advocate evidence-based health programming. D4I will guide the Directorate General of Family Planning on the nationwide rollout of an electronic management information system using domestic resources. D4I will provide technical assistance to Dhaka University to build the capacity of its junior faculty members and graduate students to develop research capacity. The activity will support the Joint Strategic Plan FY 2022-2026 (USAID and U.S. Department of State) Goal Three, with the U.S. government&apos;s Integrated Country Strategy Mission objective of Improving inclusive and equitable health, education, and livelihood services, especially for women, youth, and marginalized groups.</narrative>
  </description>
